    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-2285",
      "problem": "By finding the missing values in the ratio table below, determine the graph that represents the given relationship.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $2$ |\n| $8$ |  |\n|  | $6$ |",
      "worked_solution": "We start with the ratio ${\\color{blue}4}:{\\color{red}2}$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{{\\color{blue}4}}{{\\color{red}2}}\n$$\n\nWe can generate equivalent ratios by finding equivalent fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4\\times 2}{2\\times 2} & =\\frac{8}{4} \\\\ \\frac{4\\times 3}{2\\times 3} & =\\frac{12}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add these to our ratio table:\n\n| $x$ | $y$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $2$ |\n| $8$ | $4$ |\n| $12$ | $6$ |\n\nSo, we have the following ordered pairs: $(4,2),$ $(8,4),$ $(12,6).$\n\nPlotting these points on the coordinate plane and connecting them with a straight line, we get the following graph:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14152648/assets/8def1b37d62f91a16109db0da3287042fe5893b97bf447e6ee16946b3f8d4bfc.png)",
